{:edb/db-before-t 2311 :edb/db-after-t 2312 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535624 50 #inst "2026-10-09T03:52:15.367Z" 13194139535624 true] [17592186124490 1020 #edb/ref 17592186358079 13194139535624 true] [17592186124490 1020 #edb/ref 17592186358086 13194139535624 true] [17592186124490 1020 #edb/ref 17592186358100 13194139535624 true] [17592186124495 1020 #edb/ref 17592186358072 13194139535624 true] [17592186124495 1020 #edb/ref 17592186358093 13194139535624 true] [17592186358072 1017 #edb/ref 17592186358073 13194139535624 true] [17592186358072 1089 "q-124733" 13194139535624 true] [17592186358072 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535624 true] [17592186358072 1100 "Consider the function\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=({y}^{2}{z}^{3}-{e}^{z})\\,i+2xy{z}^{3}\\,j+(3x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}-x{e}^{z})\\,k.\n$$\n\nFind $f(x,y,z)$ such that $∇f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z).$" 13194139535624 true] [17592186358072 1113 #uuid "f6dd231c-6e98-5338-9bc2-ef1a31fa9648" 13194139535624 true] [17592186358072 1145 "The gradient of the function $f(x,y,z)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y,z)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{i}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,\\text{j}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\,\\text{k}.\n$$\n\nSince $∇f(x,y,z)=F(x,y,z),$ the function $f(x,y,z)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={y}^{2}{z}^{3}-{e}^{z},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2xy{z}^{3},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=3x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}-x{e}^{z}\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$ and $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int ({y}^{2}{z}^{3}-{e}^{z})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{y}^{2}{z}^{3}-x{e}^{z}+g(y,z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2xy{z}^{3}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y}\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2xy{z}^{3}$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2xy{z}^{3}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =2xy{z}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we integrate $\\frac{∂g}{∂y}$ with respect to $y.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(y,z) & =\\int \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\int 0\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =h(z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $g(y,z)=h(z)$ in the expression for $f(x,y,z),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=x{y}^{2}{z}^{3}-x{e}^{z}+h(z).\n$$\n\nTo determine the function $h(z),$ we differentiate $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=3x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}-x{e}^{z}+{h}^{′}(z).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=3x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}-x{e}^{z}$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}-x{e}^{z}+{h}^{′}(z) & =3x{y}^{2}{z}^{2}-x{e}^{z} \\\\ {h}^{′}(z) & =0 \\\\ h(z) & =C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=x{y}^{2}{z}^{3}-x{e}^{z}+C.\n$$" 13194139535624 true] [17592186358073 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358074 13194139535624 true] [17592186358073 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358075 13194139535624 true] [17592186358073 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358076 13194139535624 true] [17592186358073 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358077 13194139535624 true] [17592186358073 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358078 13194139535624 true] [17592186358073 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535624 true] [17592186358073 1041 "selection" 13194139535624 true] [17592186358073 1104 #edb/ref 17592186358077 13194139535624 true] [17592186358073 1110 #uuid "27d0cb5f-d94b-5736-b8d7-1396257b6194" 13194139535624 true] [17592186358074 1034 "f(x,y,z)={x}^{3}{y}^{2}+xz-{e}^{z}+C" 13194139535624 true] [17592186358074 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535624 true] [17592186358074 1111 #uuid "d17bfb9a-8e07-559b-8fac-6af97f273834" 13194139535624 true] [17592186358075 1034 "f(x,y,z)=x{y}^{2}{z}^{3}+yz-{e}^{z}+C" 13194139535624 true] [17592186358075 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535624 true] [17592186358075 1111 #uuid "43657de1-8aab-5d63-bb61-a029e159baa2" 13194139535624 true] [17592186358076 1034 "f(x,y,z)={y}^{3}z-x{e}^{z}+C" 13194139535624 true] [17592186358076 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535624 true] [17592186358076 1111 #uuid "4111b42c-485d-50ef-8134-b04c0b205a5d" 13194139535624 true] [17592186358077 1034 "f(x,y,z)=x{y}^{2}{z}^{3}-x{e}^{z}+C" 13194139535624 true] [17592186358077 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535624 true] [17592186358077 1111 #uuid "4083e5c0-fa10-5091-901b-60ddde4d0475" 13194139535624 true] [17592186358078 1034 "f(x,y,z)=xyz-y{e}^{z}+C" 13194139535624 true] [17592186358078 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535624 true] [17592186358078 1111 #uuid "ae231568-11a6-5d3b-b716-61adf9c41929" 13194139535624 true] [17592186358079 1017 #edb/ref 17592186358080 13194139535624 true] [17592186358079 1089 "q-132080" 13194139535624 true] [17592186358079 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535624 true] [17592186358079 1100 "Find $f(x,y)$ such that $∇f=F,$ where $F(x,y)={e}^{y}\\,i+(x{e}^{y}+2y)\\,j.$" 13194139535624 true] [17592186358079 1113 #uuid "56db4f7d-60e2-5a2d-b5c8-a70229b1b98b" 13194139535624 true] [17592186358079 1145 "The gradient of the function $f(x,y)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,j.\n$$\n\nSince $∇f(x,y)=F(x,y),$ the function $f(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={e}^{y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{y}+2y\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{e}^{y}+g(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{y}+{g}^{′}(y).\n$$\n\nTaking  $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{y}+2y$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x{e}^{y}+{g}^{′}(y) & =x{e}^{y}+2y \\\\ {g}^{′}(y) & =2y \\\\ g(y) & ={y}^{2}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nFinally, substituting $g(y)={y}^{2}+C$ into our expression for $f(x,y),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=x{e}^{y}+{y}^{2}+C.\n$$" 13194139535624 t