}{y})\\,i+(\\frac{x-1}{{y}^{2}})\\,j.$" 13194139535624 true] [17592186358086 1113 #uuid "a4cd2d9c-aa9c-533b-b610-fc91804dad9d" 13194139535624 true] [17592186358086 1145 "The gradient of the function $f(x,y)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,j.\n$$\n\nSince $∇f(x,y)=F(x,y),$ the function $f(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=12{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{x-1}{{y}^{2}}\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (12{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{y})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{x}^{4}-\\frac{x}{y}+g(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}+{g}^{′}(y).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{x-1}{{y}^{2}}$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}+{g}^{′}(y) & =\\frac{x-1}{{y}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}+{g}^{′}(y) & =\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}} \\\\ {g}^{′}(y) & =-\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}} \\\\ g(y) & =\\frac{1}{y}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nFinally, substituting $g(y)=\\frac{1}{y}+C$ into our expression for $f(x,y),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=3{x}^{4}-\\frac{x}{y}+\\frac{1}{y}+C.\n$$" 13194139535624 true] [17592186358087 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358088 13194139535624 true] [17592186358087 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358089 13194139535624 true] [17592186358087 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358090 13194139535624 true] [17592186358087 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358091 13194139535624 true] [17592186358087 1000 #edb/ref 17592186358092 13194139535624 true] [17592186358087 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535624 true] [17592186358087 1041 "selection" 13194139535624 true] [17592186358087 1104 #edb/ref 17592186358088 13194139535624 true] [17592186358087 1110 #uuid "f687fd7b-0748-53fe-89b3-940ba8bde874" 13194139535624 true] [175